    "yild_about_story_HENHkr": {
      "type": "yild-about-story",
      "name": "Yild About Story",
      "settings": {
        "bg_color": "#f7f5ed",
        "subtitle_color": "#4e7355",
        "title_color": "#1f3d2b",
        "text_color": "#3a4a3d",
        "subtitle": "Why we exist",
        "title": "Food is better when you know where it grew — and who grew it.",
        "story_content": "<p>Yild started with a simple frustration: supermarket \"fresh\" isn't fresh. Produce sits in cold storage for weeks while the farmers who grew it are squeezed on price. We knew both sides deserved better.</p><p>So we built a shorter route. We partner directly with local growers, collect from the farm, and deliver to your door every Sunday — no warehouses, no middlemen, no week-long waits. Farmers set fair prices and keep more of them. You get food picked at its peak, often harvested the very morning it reaches you.</p><p>And because good food should be for everyone, we donate fresh, local produce for every Vegetable Box sold — supporting families in the same communities we deliver to.</p>"
      }
    },
